\lxSVG@closescope {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>KL</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is the task-wise Kullback–Leibler divergence:
<math id="S5.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}_{T}\triangleq\mathbb{E}_{s\sim T}[D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p(\cdot\mid s)\,\|\,q(\cdot\mid s))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>KL</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}_{T}\triangleq\mathbb{E}_{s\sim T}[D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p(\cdot\mid s)\,\|\,q(\cdot\mid s))]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{D}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{D}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is the task-wise cross-entropy:
<math id="S5.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{D}_{T}\triangleq\mathbb{E}_{s\sim T}[-\sum_{x}p(x|s)\log q(x|s)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{D}_{T}\triangleq\mathbb{E}_{s\sim T}[-\sum_{x}p(x|s)\log q(x|s)]</annotation></semantics></math> (proven in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Relating Divergence and Speed-up via a Monotone Chain ‣ Appendix A Missing Proofs ‣ The Disparate Impacts of Speculative Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The result above highlights three key messages: First,
it places <math id="S5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> as the singular determinant of speculative speed-up at fixed <math id="S5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,c)</annotation></semantics></math>,
second, the task-level speedup <math id="S5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is increasing in <math id="S5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> (further corollary in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Speed-up and Acceptance Dependency ‣ Appendix A Missing Proofs ‣ The Disparate Impacts of Speculative Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>),
and third, and most importantly, task-level speed is <em id="S5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">monotone</em> in <math id="S5.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{D}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{D}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>; In particular, the above yields a monotone chain
<math id="S5.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{D}_{T}\downarrow\;\Rightarrow\;\alpha_{T}\uparrow\;\Rightarrow\;S_{T}\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">↑</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{D}_{T}\downarrow\;\Rightarrow\;\alpha_{T}\uparrow\;\Rightarrow\;S_{T}\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
            
            
            
            
            
            
            
          Throughout, we write <math id="footnote3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow x</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="footnote3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow x</annotation></semantics></math>) to represent an increase (decrease) to a scalar <math id="footnote3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>.
This has an important consequence: for fixed <math id="S5.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,c)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{D}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{D}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> provides an <em id="S5.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">optimizable</em> metric whose reduction <em id="S5.p5.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">monotonically</em> tightens a task speed-up. This rationale makes <math id="S5.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{D}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{D}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> a fitting choice for computing unfairness.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unfairness as divergence dispersions.</span> Next, the section introduces a fairness notion built on the divergence <math id="S5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{D}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{D}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, from the rightmost expression of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 5 Characterizing Unfairness in Speculative Decoding ‣ The Disparate Impacts of Speculative Decoding" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Speculative Decoding Unfairness) For a task family <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal T}=\{T_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">𝒯</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal T}=\{T_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, <em id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">speculative decoding unfairness</em> is defined as:</span></p>
